<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  WildAnimals_FeverWood.xml                 UtinniPatches — new file 2026-09-24
  ============================================================================

  Puts the campaign's Fever Wood Star-Wars-canon fauna/flora onto
  RM_FeverWood, alongside the one non-Star-Wars-donor animal row
  (VFEI2_Megathrips) and three non-Star-Wars-donor plant rows
  (AB_KeeningCordax/AB_Iashiphus/AB_Gomphoeria) that ship inline on
  src/RimMandrake/FeverWood/Defs/BiomeDefs/RM_FeverWood.xml itself, per Q9.
  Same shape as WildAnimals_Pyrelands.xml / WildAnimals_Greentide.xml.

  WHY THIS FILE HAS TO EXIST. §7 Q11a (owner, 2026-09-22): a genuinely canon
  Star Wars name is IP and must route through the Utinni campaign patch
  layer, never the franchise-free RimMandrake tier — "the top mod without
  star wars will look precisely the same as the star wars enhanced one save
  for any star wars beasts we populate it with." So RM_FeverWood may not
  carry this cast inline, and at Phase B the RUT_FeverWood twin that
  currently carries it dies and RM_FeverWood takes the tiles. Without this
  patch in place by then, the Fever Wood would lose 10 of its 11 fauna rows
  and 3 of its 7 flora rows on the live world.

  🔑 SOURCE OF TRUTH: every defName and weight below is copied from
  RUT_FeverWood.xml's own wildAnimals/wildPlants (frozen 2026-09-24), the
  roster the world runs on today, with ONE live correction: RUT_FeverWood.xml
  now casts `RSW_Nuna` (MayRequire mandrake.rsw.swbestiary), not the bare
  donor `Nuna` (MayRequire mlie.starwarsanimalcollection) that
  FEVERWOOD_RM_MOD_BUILD_1's own written table still names — that row was
  repointed to the RSW_ port by DUPLICATE_CANON_DEFNAME_PAIRS_1's owner-ruled
  merge, dated the same day (2026-09-23) as the item's own MEASURED pass, and
  this file follows the live def rather than the item's now-stale table. The
  routing verdict (Utinni patch, not inline) is unchanged either way.

  10 wildAnimals rows split by donor mod:
    mandrake.rsw.swbestiary (our own RSW_ ports):
      RSW_GlowSlug 0.5, RSW_Nuna 0.4, RSW_JewelBeetle 0.2, RSW_AcidSlug 0.05
    mlie.starwarsanimalcollection (SW canon, no port yet — DONOR_DEFS_PORT_TO_OURS_1):
      Urusai 0.5, Gelagrub 0.4, Convor 0.3, LongtailGorg 0.3, Whisperbird 0.3,
      Fambaa 0.02

  3 wildPlants rows, all mlie.starwarsanimalcollection (SW canon, no port yet):
    Plant_HydenockTree_Wild 1.5, Plant_JoganTree_Wild 0.6, Plant_Chakroot_Wild 0.4
    (hydenock/jogan/chak-root are Q11a's own worked canon examples.)

  ⚠️ A patch that matches nothing logs nothing — PatchOperationConditional
  returns true on no match, and an unmatched PatchOperationAdd is silent. A
  clean validate_patch.py run is NOT proof a row landed.
  🔴 UNVERIFIED AGAINST A LOAD: authored offline (FEVERWOOD_RM_MOD_BUILD_1
  steps 1-4). Step 5 (a scratch-world quicktest, all five expansions) is
  Desktop-only and owed — confirm all 13 rows from a post-load def dump
  before believing this file works, same standing caveat as every sibling
  WildAnimals_*.xml in this folder.

  RM_FeverWood's own inline rows (VFEI2_Megathrips, AB_KeeningCordax,
  AB_Iashiphus, AB_Gomphoeria, RM_GiantLeaf) need no patch — they are direct
  fields on the BiomeDef itself, added onto by this file, never replaced.
-->
<Patch>

  <!-- Our own RSW_ ports. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional" MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">
    <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_FeverWood"]/wildAnimals</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_FeverWood"]/wildAnimals</xpath>
      <value>
        <RSW_GlowSlug>0.5</RSW_GlowSlug>
        <RSW_Nuna>0.4</RSW_Nuna>
        <RSW_JewelBeetle>0.2</RSW_JewelBeetle>
        <RSW_AcidSlug>0.05</RSW_AcidSlug>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <!-- Star Wars canon, not yet ported to our own RSW_ defs (DONOR_DEFS_PORT_TO_OURS_1). -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional" MayRequire="mlie.starwarsanimalcollection">
    <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_FeverWood"]/wildAnimals</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_FeverWood"]/wildAnimals</xpath>
      <value>
        <Urusai>0.5</Urusai>
        <Gelagrub>0.4</Gelagrub>
        <Convor>0.3</Convor>
        <LongtailGorg>0.3</LongtailGorg>
        <Whisperbird>0.3</Whisperbird>
        <Fambaa>0.02</Fambaa>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <!-- Star Wars canon wildPlants, same donor mod, not yet ported. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional" MayRequire="mlie.starwarsanimalcollection">
    <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_FeverWood"]/wildPlants</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_FeverWood"]/wildPlants</xpath>
      <value>
        <Plant_HydenockTree_Wild>1.5</Plant_HydenockTree_Wild>
        <Plant_JoganTree_Wild>0.6</Plant_JoganTree_Wild>
        <Plant_Chakroot_Wild>0.4</Plant_Chakroot_Wild>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
